<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n43076" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Scōti</span></b>  (<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Scotti</span></b> ), ōrum,
		m., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>the
				Scots</i>, <i>a people in the northern part of
				Britain</i>, in the mod. <i>Scotland</i>,
					<i><span class="en">Amm. 27, 8, 5</span></i>; <i><span class="en">26, 4,
			5</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Hier. in Jovin. 2,
			7</span></i>.—In sing.: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Scotus, collect.,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Claud. B. Get. 417</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">id. IV. Cons. Hon. 33</span></i>;
					<i><span class="en">id. Laud. Stil. 2,
			251</span></i>.—Hence, </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>A.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Scō-tĭa</span></b> ,
				ae, f., <i>the land of
				the Scots</i>, = Hibernia, <i><span class="en">Isid. 14, 6,
				6</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>B.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Scōtĭcus</span></b> 
				(<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Scott-</span></b> ),
				a, um, adj., <i>of</i>
			or <i>belonging to Scotland</i>, <i>Scottish</i>, <i>Scotch</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">tela,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Claud. Laud. Stil. 2, 254</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
